  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "When Chef Barinov told Fedya that the inspector's wife was on him, Fedya took it as an order to seduce her. Enraged by the revelation, the inspector tries to attack before Senya knocks him out again with a vase.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Федя, ты что там творишь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Вы сказали, жена на тебе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "А я теперь всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Вы просто издеваетесь надо мной.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Ваш повар соблазнил мою жену.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Меня вы чуть не убили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Денег на самом деле нет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хватит, давайте спокойно разберёмся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Скоро нам привезут эти деньги.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И мы спокойно разойдёмся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Федя, ты вообще сейчас замолчи.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну вот видишь, мы договорились.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Федя, ты что там творишь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fedya, what are you doing over there?' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'Fedya', while 'are doing' completes the thought. Fedya answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Вы сказали, жена на тебе.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You said the wife was on me.' Fedya anchors the line on 'you', while 'to you' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "А я теперь всё понял.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And now I have understood everything.' In Russian, the idea of 'and' flows naturally into 'understood' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Вы просто издеваетесь надо мной.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are simply mocking me.' The grammar packs 'you' and 'me' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Ваш повар соблазнил мою жену.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your cook seduced my wife.' the inspector anchors the line on 'your', while 'wife' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Меня вы чуть не убили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You nearly killed me.' the inspector chooses the respectful plural 'you' alongside 'killed' to keep a polite distance.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "inspector",
      "t": "Денег на самом деле нет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There is actually no money at all.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'money' before landing on 'no'. Chef Barinov answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Хватит, давайте спокойно разберёмся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Enough, let us sort this out calmly.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'enough' before landing on 'to sort out'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Скоро нам привезут эти деньги.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Soon they will bring us this money.' Chef Barinov anchors the line on 'soon', while 'money' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "И мы спокойно разойдёмся.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And we will part ways peacefully.' Notice the reflexive suffix on the verb meaning 'we will part ways', turning the action back on the subject.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Федя, ты вообще сейчас замолчи.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Fedya, you be quiet altogether right now.' Chef Barinov brings out the contrast between 'Fedya' and 'you' in a few short words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну вот видишь, мы договорились.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Well, you see, we reached an agreement.' The grammar packs 'come on' and 'agreed' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
